gamescope-tegra license scope
============================

This source distribution contains components under several licenses.
It is not a BSD-only distribution and it does not relicense upstream files.

The combined Gamescope program with the Tegra implementation is distributed
under GNU General Public License version 2. The complete text is in COPYING
and LICENSES/GPL-2.0.txt. Individual Tegra files marked GPL-2.0-or-later retain
their permission to use that file under version 2 or a later version.

Original upstream Gamescope files retain their original licenses and notices.
The complete upstream Gamescope license, including the OpenColorIO and ReShade
notices, is preserved in gamescope/LICENSE and LICENSES/Gamescope.upstream.txt.
Other third-party components retain their own licenses and copyright notices.
For components explicitly offered under Apache-2.0 OR MIT, this distribution
selects the MIT alternative. This choice does not apply to Apache-only files.

Original project packaging scripts, tests, integration examples and documents
outside gamescope/, where not derived from another component, are licensed
under GPL-2.0-or-later: GNU GPL version 2 or, at your option, any later version.
The full version 2 text is in COPYING. This matches the grant in gman's source
notice; it does not grant broader rights over GPL-2.0-only third-party material.
Modified/generated/upstream-derived
material instead retains its source component's license. In particular the
experimental EGLStream patch has the GPL scope of the Tegra code it modifies.

See NOTICE.md, docs/LICENSING.md and docs/PROVENANCE.md for component scope,
attribution, source origins and the boundaries of this source-only package.
Proprietary runtime dependencies are not included or covered by this license.

